# the row of Reflect.apply takes a function and an object. Where both are proven by what makes them, the call is forwarded. Where one is not, is left out or is something else, the built-in is called, which refuses in its own words
# RUN: walk f2 f3 f4 f5 mechanisms=none
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK-NOT: CallList
# CHECK: = Call {{*}} calleeName="Reflect.apply" [isDoneInPlace]
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK: [[callee]]: f1 {{*}} = NewClosure function=f1
# CHECK: [[list]]: Array @Cell = NewArray
# CHECK: [[boxed]]: f1 @JSValue = Box [[callee]]
# CHECK: = CallList [[boxed]], {{*}}, [[list]] calleeName="Reflect.apply"
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK: = Call {{*}} calleeName="Reflect.apply" [isDoneInPlace]
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK-NOT: CallList
# CHECK: = Call {{*}} calleeName="Reflect.apply" [isDoneInPlace]
# RUN(NEVER): walk f3 mechanisms=none
# NEVER-NOT: isDoneInPlace
# PROGRAM-OF: ../../answers/reflect-apply-done-in-place-keeps-what-the-built-in-refuses.ir
